    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Zadok the priest, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, Nathan the prophet, Shimei, Rei, and the mighty men who belonged to David, were not with Adonijah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "but he didn’t call Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah, and the mighty men, and Solomon his brother."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Nathan spoke to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon, saying, “Haven’t you heard that Adonijah the son of Haggith reigns, and David our lord doesn’t know it?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "Behold, while she was still talking with the king, Nathan the prophet came in."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "They told the king, saying, “Behold, Nathan the prophet!” When he had come in before the king, he bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nathan said, “My lord, King, have you said, ‘Adonijah shall reign after me, and he shall sit on my throne’?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "King David said, “Call to me Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada.” They came before the king."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "Let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him there king over Israel. Blow the trumpet, and say, ‘Long live King Solomon!’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:38",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites and the Pelethites went down and had Solomon ride on King David’s mule, and brought him to Gihon."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:44",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king has sent with him Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and they have caused him to ride on the king’s mule."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 1:45",
        "textualBasisJa": "Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet have anointed him king in Gihon. They have come up from there rejoicing, so that the city rang again. This is the noise that you have heard."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1KI 4:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "Azariah the son of Nathan was over the officers; Zabud the son of Nathan was chief minister, the king’s friend;"
      }
    ],
